        "root_concepts": "[ship structures]",
        "section": "naval-architecture",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Ship Structures",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Where weight > buoyancy locally -> the beam wants to sag there.\n   Where buoyancy > weight locally -> the beam wants to hog there.\n   The MISMATCH between the weight curve and buoyancy curve = the load\n   that bends the entire ship. Integrate it twice -> bending moment.\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-SHIP-STRUCTURES.md#007",
      "path": [
        "04-SHIP-STRUCTURES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:naval-architecture:04-ship-structures, git-history:naval-architecture:04-ship-structures]",
        "canonical_path": "naval-architecture/04-SHIP-STRUCTURES.md",
        "concepts": "[hull girder, longitudinal strength, hogging, sagging, scantlings, marine materials]",
        "current_path": "naval-architecture/04-SHIP-STRUCTURES.md",
        "id": "maxim:naval-architecture:ship-structures",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "naval-architecture",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[ship structures]",
        "section": "naval-architecture",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Ship Structures",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The entire longitudinal-strength problem is this: weight and buoyancy are both\ndistributed along the length but *not in the same way*, and their difference bends the\nship. Everything else is bookkeeping on that idea."
    },
