      "text": "## Layer 1: Longitudinal Strength — Hogging and Sagging"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-SHIP-STRUCTURES.md#010",
      "path": [
        "04-SHIP-STRUCTURES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:naval-architecture:04-ship-structures, git-history:naval-architecture:04-ship-structures]",
        "canonical_path": "naval-architecture/04-SHIP-STRUCTURES.md",
        "concepts": "[hull girder, longitudinal strength, hogging, sagging, scantlings, marine materials]",
        "current_path": "naval-architecture/04-SHIP-STRUCTURES.md",
        "id": "maxim:naval-architecture:ship-structures",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "naval-architecture",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[ship structures]",
        "section": "naval-architecture",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Ship Structures",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Sum weight and buoyancy at each station along the length. Their difference is the **load\ncurve** q(x). Integrate q(x) once to get the **shear force** Q(x); integrate again to get\nthe **bending moment** M(x). This is ordinary Euler-Bernoulli beam theory (`structural/`),\napplied to a floating beam. The two extreme load cases have names."
    },
    {
      "id": "04-SHIP-STRUCTURES.md#011",
      "path": [
        "04-SHIP-STRUCTURES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:naval-architecture:04-ship-structures, git-history:naval-architecture:04-ship-structures]",
        "canonical_path": "naval-architecture/04-SHIP-STRUCTURES.md",
        "concepts": "[hull girder, longitudinal strength, hogging, sagging, scantlings, marine materials]",
        "current_path": "naval-architecture/04-SHIP-STRUCTURES.md",
        "id": "maxim:naval-architecture:ship-structures",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "naval-architecture",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[ship structures]",
        "section": "naval-architecture",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Ship Structures",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nHOGGING vs SAGGING (the two governing wave conditions)\n==============================================================================="
    },
    {
