      },
      "text": "The headline design equation is **σ = M / Z**: the bending stress in the deck or bottom\nequals the bending moment divided by the section modulus. Design controls two things: keep\nM down (it is largely fixed by ship size and the sea, though loading discipline matters) and\nmake Z big (concentrate steel far from the neutral axis — the deck and bottom — exactly\nwhere a wide-flange I-beam puts its material)."
    },
    {
